    "result_text": "All 268 tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `registrationDate` feature for owners: when an owner is created without a registration date, it defaults to today's date and is returned in the owner response as `registrationDate` in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. The `spring` generator maps `format: date` to `java.time.LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`. Since `Owner` extends `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the field appears in the response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 In `saveOwner`, set `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it's null.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (required since the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none` and initializes from `schema.sql`).\n\nMapStruct auto-maps the same-named `registrationDate` property in both directions, so no mapper changes were needed. The `Cp08Tests` acceptance test and all 268 tests pass.",
